    "knowledge_point": "Identifying the Shift Applied to an Exponential Growth Curve",
    "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930907/assets/8764149ca0000522277d48bf48f4ef14ba06f7e4793ba1a58ef639ff7af3a3b9.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y={3}^{x}+c.$ Determine the value of $c$ and find the equation of the curve.",
    "worked_solution": "The horizontal asymptote of $y={3}^{x}$ is $y=0.$ The vertical translation $y={3}^{x}+c$ shifts the asymptote to $y=c.$\n\nIn the graph above, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-2.$ Therefore, $c=-2.$",
